content:
The invoice row for ORD-00974 was created at t=476 (after the v1.1 deploy at t=461), and the VAT value (2889.9) is wildly wrong — it looks like the new extraction prompt misread the invoice text and extracted a wrong number as VAT. The fault clearly originates in invoice-agent, not sync-job. Let me check the source invoice text to confirm bad extraction vs. a bad input document.

```json
{
  "investigate": [
    {
      "tool": "sql",
      "query": "SELECT id, supplier, invoice_text, status, created_at FROM orders WHERE id = 'ORD-00974'",
      "why": "Inspect the raw invoice_text for ORD-00974 to determine whether the VAT figure of 2889.9 appears in the source document (bad_input) or whether the new extraction prompt hallucinated/misread a correct document (bad_deploy)."
    }
  ],
  "hypotheses": [],
  "summary": "Investigating the source invoice text for ORD-00974 to distinguish a bad_deploy (prompt misreads a valid document) from bad_input (the document itself contains a wrong VAT figure)."
}
```
